{"title":"DSE Shoulder R1/L1 and Bumper R2/L2 Omoron Switch Buttons","slug":"DSE-Shoulder-R1-L1-and-Bumper-R2-L2-Omoron-Switch-Buttons","date":"2026-07-24T02:10:32.000Z","updated":"2026-07-24T08:56:52.138Z","comments":true,"path":"api/articles/DSE-Shoulder-R1-L1-and-Bumper-R2-L2-Omoron-Switch-Buttons.json","excerpt":" [Figure] PS5精英双肩键微动双扳机微动安装, 扳机固定微动与双切扳机方案(英文版)","covers":["https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724101259878.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724141538917.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724114841882.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724102748232.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151322900.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724152218917.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724144213209.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724114734688.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724144425428.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724150639459.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724152423497.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724114945950.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724115011292.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151454943.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724150312866.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151046829.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724150112686.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151159068.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151848275.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724150813298.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151551757.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724153817776.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724153749944.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724155412518.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724154042887.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724154138473.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724155802708.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160812707.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160950908.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724161507411.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724161536670.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724161745813.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724161922448.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160356310.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160426848.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160443011.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724144213209.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724162645383.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724162614644.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724162830515.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724163028129.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724163539004.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724163341381.png","https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724163128415.png"],"content":"<img class=\"lozad\" data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724101259878.png\">\n\n<p>DSE Shoulder R1&#x2F;L1 and Bumper R2&#x2F;L2 Omoron Switch Buttons<br>Install Omoron Switch Buttons for DSE Shoulder R1&#x2F;L1 Bumper R2&#x2F;L2<br>PS5精英双肩键微动双扳机微动安装, 扳机固定微动与双切扳机方案(英文版)</p>\n<span id=\"more\"></span>\n\n<h1 id=\"Installation-Steps\"><a href=\"#Installation-Steps\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"Installation Steps\"></a>Installation Steps</h1><h2 id=\"1-Shoulder-L1-R1-Omoron-Switch-Buttons\"><a href=\"#1-Shoulder-L1-R1-Omoron-Switch-Buttons\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"1. Shoulder L1&#x2F;R1 Omoron Switch Buttons\"></a>1. Shoulder L1&#x2F;R1 Omoron Switch Buttons</h2><h3 id=\"1-1-Disassembly-DSE\"><a href=\"#1-1-Disassembly-DSE\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"1.1 Disassembly DSE\"></a>1.1 Disassembly DSE</h3><p>Prepare L1&#x2F;R1 Omoron Switch: Cut off the metal contacts at both ends of the microswitch.</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724141538917.png\" alt=\"image-20260724141538917\"></p>\n<p>Soldering jumper wires</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724114841882.png\" alt=\"image-20260724114841882\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"1-2-Put-in-the-Omoron-Switch\"><a href=\"#1-2-Put-in-the-Omoron-Switch\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"1.2 Put in the Omoron Switch\"></a>1.2 Put in the Omoron Switch</h3><p>Put it in to the location of shoulder, tilt the Omron Switch in the suite location(inside of the module) like below</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724102748232.png\" alt=\"image-20260724102748232\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151322900.png\" alt=\"image-20260724151322900\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"1-3-Link-the-wire-from-Omoron-Switch-to-the-mini-board-of-the-module\"><a href=\"#1-3-Link-the-wire-from-Omoron-Switch-to-the-mini-board-of-the-module\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"1.3 Link the wire(from Omoron Switch) to the mini-board of the module\"></a>1.3 Link the wire(from Omoron Switch) to the mini-board of the module</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724152218917.png\" alt=\"image-20260724152218917\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724144213209.png\" alt=\"image-20260724144213209\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724114734688.png\" alt=\"image-20260724114734688\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724144425428.png\" alt=\"image-20260724144425428\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724150639459.png\" alt=\"image-20260724150639459\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724152423497.png\" alt=\"image-20260724152423497\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"1-4-optional-Special-customization\"><a href=\"#1-4-optional-Special-customization\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"1.4 [optional]Special customization\"></a>1.4 [optional]Special customization</h3><p>If we ONLY need Omoron Switch on Shoulder L1&#x2F;R1(and not changes to the Bumpers L2&#x2F;R2), we need to cut the Conductive adhesive in below shape: </p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724114945950.png\" alt=\"image-20260724114945950\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724115011292.png\" alt=\"image-20260724115011292\"></p>\n<h2 id=\"2-Bumper-L2-R2-Micro-Switch-Buttons\"><a href=\"#2-Bumper-L2-R2-Micro-Switch-Buttons\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"2. Bumper L2&#x2F;R2 Micro-Switch Buttons\"></a>2. Bumper L2&#x2F;R2 Micro-Switch Buttons</h2><p>Disassembly DSE</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151454943.png\" alt=\"image-20260724151454943\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"2-1-Prepare-L2-R2-Omoron-Switch\"><a href=\"#2-1-Prepare-L2-R2-Omoron-Switch\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"2.1 Prepare L2&#x2F;R2 Omoron Switch\"></a>2.1 Prepare L2&#x2F;R2 Omoron Switch</h3><p>Soldering 2 jumper wires on both end of Micro-Switch</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724150312866.png\" alt=\"image-20260724150312866\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"2-2-Put-in-the-Omoron-Switch-in-3D-printing-helper\"><a href=\"#2-2-Put-in-the-Omoron-Switch-in-3D-printing-helper\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"2.2 Put in the Omoron Switch in 3D printing helper\"></a>2.2 Put in the Omoron Switch in 3D printing helper</h3><p>And put in the 3D printing helper to the module</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151046829.png\" alt=\"image-20260724151046829\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724150112686.png\" alt=\"image-20260724150112686\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151159068.png\" alt=\"image-20260724151159068\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"2-3-Link-the-wire-from-Omoron-Switch-to-the-mini-board-of-the-module\"><a href=\"#2-3-Link-the-wire-from-Omoron-Switch-to-the-mini-board-of-the-module\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"2.3 Link the wire(from Omoron Switch) to the mini-board of the module\"></a>2.3 Link the wire(from Omoron Switch) to the mini-board of the module</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151848275.png\" alt=\"image-20260724151848275\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724150813298.png\" alt=\"image-20260724150813298\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151551757.png\" alt=\"image-20260724151551757\"></p>\n<h2 id=\"3-Bumper-L2-R2-Micro-switch-double-stage-Advance\"><a href=\"#3-Bumper-L2-R2-Micro-switch-double-stage-Advance\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3. Bumper L2&#x2F;R2 Micro-switch double-stage(Advance)\"></a>3. Bumper L2&#x2F;R2 Micro-switch double-stage(Advance)</h2><p>Need special addtitional 3D priting helper for double-stage switch between original Bumper and Omoron Switch Bumper.</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724153817776.png\" alt=\"image-20260724153817776\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724153749944.png\" alt=\"image-20260724153749944\"></p>\n<p>There is 3 positiions for Edge’s L2 R2 Bumper<br>first position: it has large room to push&#x2F;trigger; stay original<br>second position: it has mid room to trigger; stay original</p>\n<p>last position:<br>    Original: small room;<br>    Now: becomes omoron switch to trigger&#x2F;click</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-1-Prepare-2-Omoron-Switch\"><a href=\"#3-1-Prepare-2-Omoron-Switch\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.1 Prepare 2 Omoron Switch\"></a>3.1 Prepare 2 Omoron Switch</h3><p>Prepare L1&#x2F;R1 Omoron Switch: Cut off the metal contacts at both ends of the microswitch.</p>\n<p>After done cutting the little metal at the both end of Micro-Switch, AFTER the little metal cut, cut additional plastic near the white trigger point. See blelow in detail:</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724155412518.png\" alt=\"image-20260724155412518\"></p>\n<p>Soldering 2 jumper wires on the both point of Omoron switch</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-2-Disassembly-DSE’s-Bumper-module\"><a href=\"#3-2-Disassembly-DSE’s-Bumper-module\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.2 Disassembly DSE’s Bumper module\"></a>3.2 Disassembly DSE’s Bumper module</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724154042887.png\" alt=\"image-20260724154042887\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724154138473.png\" alt=\"image-20260724154138473\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"3-3-Put-Replace-the-3D-helper-into-the-Bumper-module-and-lock-it\"><a href=\"#3-3-Put-Replace-the-3D-helper-into-the-Bumper-module-and-lock-it\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.3 Put&#x2F;Replace the 3D helper into the Bumper module and lock it\"></a>3.3 Put&#x2F;Replace the 3D helper into the Bumper module and lock it</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724155802708.png\" alt=\"image-20260724155802708\"></p>\n<p>test the location and move the switchs between 3 different position, make sure the move is smooth</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-4-Put-in-the-Omoron-Switch-into-the-3D-helper-and-lock-it-using-glue\"><a href=\"#3-4-Put-in-the-Omoron-Switch-into-the-3D-helper-and-lock-it-using-glue\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.4 Put in the Omoron Switch into the 3D helper and lock it using glue\"></a>3.4 Put in the Omoron Switch into the 3D helper and lock it using glue</h3><p>Use few glue at the back of Omoron switch and put it in the 3D printing helper; so the Omron switch will be locked, stay at the right location.(see above image, and there will be 2 wires at both end of customizaed&#x2F;cutted Omoron switch)</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-5-Cut-the-Bumper-cap\"><a href=\"#3-5-Cut-the-Bumper-cap\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.5 Cut the Bumper cap\"></a>3.5 Cut the Bumper cap</h3><p>Original: <img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160812707.png\" alt=\"image-20260724160812707\"></p>\n<p>The white little 3D printing helper is used to put in the hole of the Bumper cap</p>\n<p>Cut the cap: </p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160950908.png\" alt=\"image-20260724160950908\"></p>\n<p>We cut the cap since the original cap will be stuck by the omoron switch, after the cut, all three positions of the bumper will not touching the Omoron switch body.</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724161507411.png\" alt=\"image-20260724161507411\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724161536670.png\" alt=\"image-20260724161536670\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724161745813.png\" alt=\"image-20260724161745813\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"3-6-Put-the-3D-printing-helper-in-the-Bumper-cap\"><a href=\"#3-6-Put-the-3D-printing-helper-in-the-Bumper-cap\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.6 Put the 3D printing helper in the Bumper cap\"></a>3.6 Put the 3D printing helper in the Bumper cap</h3><p>We will use the 3D printing little helper to touch&#x2F;click the Omoron switch, </p>\n<p>use few glue at the hole of bumper cap to lock the white 3D printing little helper with the bumper cap.</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724161922448.png\" alt=\"image-20260724161922448\"></p>\n<p>This small white 3D printing helper will touch the Omron Switch white point for triggering.</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-7-Assembly-the-Bumper-module-to-test-3-different-position-of-the-switch\"><a href=\"#3-7-Assembly-the-Bumper-module-to-test-3-different-position-of-the-switch\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.7 Assembly the Bumper module to test 3 different position of the switch\"></a>3.7 Assembly the Bumper module to test 3 different position of the switch</h3><p>See below 3 different positions:</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160356310.png\" alt=\"image-20260724160356310\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160426848.png\" alt=\"image-20260724160426848\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160443011.png\" alt=\"image-20260724160443011\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"3-8-Glue-the-wire-gently-and-link-it-to-micro-board-of-Bumper\"><a href=\"#3-8-Glue-the-wire-gently-and-link-it-to-micro-board-of-Bumper\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.8 Glue the wire gently and link it to micro-board of Bumper\"></a>3.8 Glue the wire gently and link it to micro-board of Bumper</h3><p>Omoron switch’s 1 wire link to L2&#x2F;R2, another wire link to GND</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724144213209.png\" alt=\"image-20260724144213209\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724162645383.png\" alt=\"image-20260724162645383\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"3-9-Assemble-the-Bumper-using-original-screws\"><a href=\"#3-9-Assemble-the-Bumper-using-original-screws\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.9 Assemble the Bumper using original screws\"></a>3.9 Assemble the Bumper using original screws</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724162614644.png\" alt=\"image-20260724162614644\"></p>\n<p>Aseembly it and test the three different location of the Bumper switch</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724162830515.png\" alt=\"image-20260724162830515\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"3-10-Cut-the-back-shell-of-the-DSE-for-the-new-Bumper\"><a href=\"#3-10-Cut-the-back-shell-of-the-DSE-for-the-new-Bumper\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.10 Cut the back shell of the DSE for the new Bumper\"></a>3.10 Cut the back shell of the DSE for the new Bumper</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724163028129.png\" alt=\"image-20260724163028129\"></p>\n<p>Cut the position of both hole for both Bumpers</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724163539004.png\" alt=\"image-20260724163539004\"></p>\n<p>Use this step of cutting to make sure the bumper smooth switches between 3 different position of switches.</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-11-Assemble-and-test\"><a href=\"#3-11-Assemble-and-test\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.11 Assemble and test\"></a>3.11 Assemble and test</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724163341381.png\" alt=\"image-20260724163341381\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724163128415.png\" alt=\"image-20260724163128415\"></p>\n","more":"<h1 id=\"Installation-Steps\"><a href=\"#Installation-Steps\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"Installation Steps\"></a>Installation Steps</h1><h2 id=\"1-Shoulder-L1-R1-Omoron-Switch-Buttons\"><a href=\"#1-Shoulder-L1-R1-Omoron-Switch-Buttons\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"1. Shoulder L1&#x2F;R1 Omoron Switch Buttons\"></a>1. Shoulder L1&#x2F;R1 Omoron Switch Buttons</h2><h3 id=\"1-1-Disassembly-DSE\"><a href=\"#1-1-Disassembly-DSE\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"1.1 Disassembly DSE\"></a>1.1 Disassembly DSE</h3><p>Prepare L1&#x2F;R1 Omoron Switch: Cut off the metal contacts at both ends of the microswitch.</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724141538917.png\" alt=\"image-20260724141538917\"></p>\n<p>Soldering jumper wires</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724114841882.png\" alt=\"image-20260724114841882\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"1-2-Put-in-the-Omoron-Switch\"><a href=\"#1-2-Put-in-the-Omoron-Switch\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"1.2 Put in the Omoron Switch\"></a>1.2 Put in the Omoron Switch</h3><p>Put it in to the location of shoulder, tilt the Omron Switch in the suite location(inside of the module) like below</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724102748232.png\" alt=\"image-20260724102748232\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151322900.png\" alt=\"image-20260724151322900\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"1-3-Link-the-wire-from-Omoron-Switch-to-the-mini-board-of-the-module\"><a href=\"#1-3-Link-the-wire-from-Omoron-Switch-to-the-mini-board-of-the-module\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"1.3 Link the wire(from Omoron Switch) to the mini-board of the module\"></a>1.3 Link the wire(from Omoron Switch) to the mini-board of the module</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724152218917.png\" alt=\"image-20260724152218917\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724144213209.png\" alt=\"image-20260724144213209\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724114734688.png\" alt=\"image-20260724114734688\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724144425428.png\" alt=\"image-20260724144425428\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724150639459.png\" alt=\"image-20260724150639459\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724152423497.png\" alt=\"image-20260724152423497\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"1-4-optional-Special-customization\"><a href=\"#1-4-optional-Special-customization\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"1.4 [optional]Special customization\"></a>1.4 [optional]Special customization</h3><p>If we ONLY need Omoron Switch on Shoulder L1&#x2F;R1(and not changes to the Bumpers L2&#x2F;R2), we need to cut the Conductive adhesive in below shape: </p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724114945950.png\" alt=\"image-20260724114945950\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724115011292.png\" alt=\"image-20260724115011292\"></p>\n<h2 id=\"2-Bumper-L2-R2-Micro-Switch-Buttons\"><a href=\"#2-Bumper-L2-R2-Micro-Switch-Buttons\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"2. Bumper L2&#x2F;R2 Micro-Switch Buttons\"></a>2. Bumper L2&#x2F;R2 Micro-Switch Buttons</h2><p>Disassembly DSE</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151454943.png\" alt=\"image-20260724151454943\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"2-1-Prepare-L2-R2-Omoron-Switch\"><a href=\"#2-1-Prepare-L2-R2-Omoron-Switch\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"2.1 Prepare L2&#x2F;R2 Omoron Switch\"></a>2.1 Prepare L2&#x2F;R2 Omoron Switch</h3><p>Soldering 2 jumper wires on both end of Micro-Switch</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724150312866.png\" alt=\"image-20260724150312866\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"2-2-Put-in-the-Omoron-Switch-in-3D-printing-helper\"><a href=\"#2-2-Put-in-the-Omoron-Switch-in-3D-printing-helper\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"2.2 Put in the Omoron Switch in 3D printing helper\"></a>2.2 Put in the Omoron Switch in 3D printing helper</h3><p>And put in the 3D printing helper to the module</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151046829.png\" alt=\"image-20260724151046829\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724150112686.png\" alt=\"image-20260724150112686\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151159068.png\" alt=\"image-20260724151159068\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"2-3-Link-the-wire-from-Omoron-Switch-to-the-mini-board-of-the-module\"><a href=\"#2-3-Link-the-wire-from-Omoron-Switch-to-the-mini-board-of-the-module\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"2.3 Link the wire(from Omoron Switch) to the mini-board of the module\"></a>2.3 Link the wire(from Omoron Switch) to the mini-board of the module</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151848275.png\" alt=\"image-20260724151848275\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724150813298.png\" alt=\"image-20260724150813298\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724151551757.png\" alt=\"image-20260724151551757\"></p>\n<h2 id=\"3-Bumper-L2-R2-Micro-switch-double-stage-Advance\"><a href=\"#3-Bumper-L2-R2-Micro-switch-double-stage-Advance\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3. Bumper L2&#x2F;R2 Micro-switch double-stage(Advance)\"></a>3. Bumper L2&#x2F;R2 Micro-switch double-stage(Advance)</h2><p>Need special addtitional 3D priting helper for double-stage switch between original Bumper and Omoron Switch Bumper.</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724153817776.png\" alt=\"image-20260724153817776\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724153749944.png\" alt=\"image-20260724153749944\"></p>\n<p>There is 3 positiions for Edge’s L2 R2 Bumper<br>first position: it has large room to push&#x2F;trigger; stay original<br>second position: it has mid room to trigger; stay original</p>\n<p>last position:<br>    Original: small room;<br>    Now: becomes omoron switch to trigger&#x2F;click</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-1-Prepare-2-Omoron-Switch\"><a href=\"#3-1-Prepare-2-Omoron-Switch\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.1 Prepare 2 Omoron Switch\"></a>3.1 Prepare 2 Omoron Switch</h3><p>Prepare L1&#x2F;R1 Omoron Switch: Cut off the metal contacts at both ends of the microswitch.</p>\n<p>After done cutting the little metal at the both end of Micro-Switch, AFTER the little metal cut, cut additional plastic near the white trigger point. See blelow in detail:</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724155412518.png\" alt=\"image-20260724155412518\"></p>\n<p>Soldering 2 jumper wires on the both point of Omoron switch</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-2-Disassembly-DSE’s-Bumper-module\"><a href=\"#3-2-Disassembly-DSE’s-Bumper-module\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.2 Disassembly DSE’s Bumper module\"></a>3.2 Disassembly DSE’s Bumper module</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724154042887.png\" alt=\"image-20260724154042887\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724154138473.png\" alt=\"image-20260724154138473\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"3-3-Put-Replace-the-3D-helper-into-the-Bumper-module-and-lock-it\"><a href=\"#3-3-Put-Replace-the-3D-helper-into-the-Bumper-module-and-lock-it\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.3 Put&#x2F;Replace the 3D helper into the Bumper module and lock it\"></a>3.3 Put&#x2F;Replace the 3D helper into the Bumper module and lock it</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724155802708.png\" alt=\"image-20260724155802708\"></p>\n<p>test the location and move the switchs between 3 different position, make sure the move is smooth</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-4-Put-in-the-Omoron-Switch-into-the-3D-helper-and-lock-it-using-glue\"><a href=\"#3-4-Put-in-the-Omoron-Switch-into-the-3D-helper-and-lock-it-using-glue\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.4 Put in the Omoron Switch into the 3D helper and lock it using glue\"></a>3.4 Put in the Omoron Switch into the 3D helper and lock it using glue</h3><p>Use few glue at the back of Omoron switch and put it in the 3D printing helper; so the Omron switch will be locked, stay at the right location.(see above image, and there will be 2 wires at both end of customizaed&#x2F;cutted Omoron switch)</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-5-Cut-the-Bumper-cap\"><a href=\"#3-5-Cut-the-Bumper-cap\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.5 Cut the Bumper cap\"></a>3.5 Cut the Bumper cap</h3><p>Original: <img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160812707.png\" alt=\"image-20260724160812707\"></p>\n<p>The white little 3D printing helper is used to put in the hole of the Bumper cap</p>\n<p>Cut the cap: </p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160950908.png\" alt=\"image-20260724160950908\"></p>\n<p>We cut the cap since the original cap will be stuck by the omoron switch, after the cut, all three positions of the bumper will not touching the Omoron switch body.</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724161507411.png\" alt=\"image-20260724161507411\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724161536670.png\" alt=\"image-20260724161536670\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724161745813.png\" alt=\"image-20260724161745813\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"3-6-Put-the-3D-printing-helper-in-the-Bumper-cap\"><a href=\"#3-6-Put-the-3D-printing-helper-in-the-Bumper-cap\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.6 Put the 3D printing helper in the Bumper cap\"></a>3.6 Put the 3D printing helper in the Bumper cap</h3><p>We will use the 3D printing little helper to touch&#x2F;click the Omoron switch, </p>\n<p>use few glue at the hole of bumper cap to lock the white 3D printing little helper with the bumper cap.</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724161922448.png\" alt=\"image-20260724161922448\"></p>\n<p>This small white 3D printing helper will touch the Omron Switch white point for triggering.</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-7-Assembly-the-Bumper-module-to-test-3-different-position-of-the-switch\"><a href=\"#3-7-Assembly-the-Bumper-module-to-test-3-different-position-of-the-switch\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.7 Assembly the Bumper module to test 3 different position of the switch\"></a>3.7 Assembly the Bumper module to test 3 different position of the switch</h3><p>See below 3 different positions:</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160356310.png\" alt=\"image-20260724160356310\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160426848.png\" alt=\"image-20260724160426848\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724160443011.png\" alt=\"image-20260724160443011\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"3-8-Glue-the-wire-gently-and-link-it-to-micro-board-of-Bumper\"><a href=\"#3-8-Glue-the-wire-gently-and-link-it-to-micro-board-of-Bumper\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.8 Glue the wire gently and link it to micro-board of Bumper\"></a>3.8 Glue the wire gently and link it to micro-board of Bumper</h3><p>Omoron switch’s 1 wire link to L2&#x2F;R2, another wire link to GND</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724144213209.png\" alt=\"image-20260724144213209\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724162645383.png\" alt=\"image-20260724162645383\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"3-9-Assemble-the-Bumper-using-original-screws\"><a href=\"#3-9-Assemble-the-Bumper-using-original-screws\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.9 Assemble the Bumper using original screws\"></a>3.9 Assemble the Bumper using original screws</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724162614644.png\" alt=\"image-20260724162614644\"></p>\n<p>Aseembly it and test the three different location of the Bumper switch</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724162830515.png\" alt=\"image-20260724162830515\"></p>\n<h3 id=\"3-10-Cut-the-back-shell-of-the-DSE-for-the-new-Bumper\"><a href=\"#3-10-Cut-the-back-shell-of-the-DSE-for-the-new-Bumper\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.10 Cut the back shell of the DSE for the new Bumper\"></a>3.10 Cut the back shell of the DSE for the new Bumper</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724163028129.png\" alt=\"image-20260724163028129\"></p>\n<p>Cut the position of both hole for both Bumpers</p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724163539004.png\" alt=\"image-20260724163539004\"></p>\n<p>Use this step of cutting to make sure the bumper smooth switches between 3 different position of switches.</p>\n<h3 id=\"3-11-Assemble-and-test\"><a href=\"#3-11-Assemble-and-test\" class=\"headerlink\" title=\"3.11 Assemble and test\"></a>3.11 Assemble and test</h3><p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724163341381.png\" alt=\"image-20260724163341381\"></p>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://img.carlzeng.com:3/i/2026/07/image-20260724163128415.png\" alt=\"image-20260724163128415\"></p>","categories":[{"name":"DSE","path":"api/categories/DSE.json"}],"tags":[{"name":"DSE","path":"api/tags/DSE.json"},{"name":"Omoron","path":"api/tags/Omoron.json"},{"name":"Switch","path":"api/tags/Switch.json"}]}